===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|recreacion}}; equivalent to {{affix|en|re-|creation}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|re-creation}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{a|en|UK}} {{enPR|rē-krē-āʹshən}}, {{IPA|en|/ɹiːkɹiˈeɪʃən/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-recreation (recreate).wav|Audio (Southern England)}}
* {{a|en|US}} {{enPR|rē-krē-āʹshən}}, {{IPA|en|/ɹiːkɹiˈeɪʃən/}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪʃən|s=4}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# The process of creating something again.
# The result of this process.

=====Usage notes=====
The hyphenated form {{m|en|re-creation}} avoids confusion with the more common other sense.

